      "hook": "Close-up on Alexander's hands holding an official War Office document bundle sealed with red wax and ribbon, stamped 'WAR OFFICE - TOP SECRET' with the royal crest.",
      "cliffhanger": "The Crown Official reads the damning names: 'Lord Henry Sterling. Rupert Ashburn.' The camera cuts to Rupert's horrified eyes darting in sheer terror.",
      "why": "Starts on a shocking piece of evidence and builds to the public naming of the traitors, ending on the villain's terror before any resolution.",
      "context_gap": "A stranger may not know Alexander is the true Duke or that Rupert stole his title, but the visual authority and the official reading make the stakes clear."
    },
    {
      "title": "The Guards Defy the Usurper",
      "start_block": "B008",
      "end_block": "B019",
      "hook": "Extreme close-up on Rupert's furious face, veins bulging at his temples, as he screams 'I said arrest him!'",
      "cliffhanger": "The Guard Captain snaps a crisp salute toward Alexander and says 'No. He is your Duke.'",
      "why": "Opens on a screaming villain, then delivers the shocking reversal where the guards refuse him and salute the true Duke, ending on the power shift.",
      "context_gap": "A stranger may not know Alexander is the rightful Duke, but the guard's salute and the line 'He is your Duke' make the allegiance clear."
    },
    {
      "title": "The Traitor's Escape Is Blocked",
      "start_block": "B077",
      "end_block": "B086",
      "hook": "Rupert whirls around in a frenzy, pointing his finger toward Lord Sterling and screaming 'Sterling handled the report!'",
      "cliffhanger": "Lord Sterling pulls open the church door to escape, only to find a stern Police Constable standing directly outside, blocking the passage: 'Going somewhere, Lord Sterling?'",
      "why": "Starts on a frantic betrayal accusation, then cuts on the moment the escape is blocked, leaving the traitor's fate hanging.",
      "context_gap": "A stranger may not know Lord Sterling's full role in the conspiracy, but the accusation and the police blockade make the threat clear."
